      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T20:19:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s because we\u0027re working on a list API, which is kinda weird. Line 41 needs target.domain_id which is the domain ID from a domain-scoped token. Because we\u0027re not passing a project_id or anything like as a target, we can\u0027t use something like %(target.project.domain_id)s, since there isn\u0027t a project involved in this request.\n\nLine 41 is really just a way to ensure we require either a system-scoped token or a project-scoped token if someone is using the defaults.\n\nLine 46 is actually getting used on the GET /v3/projects/{project_id} API, so we can make assertions about the project in the request. If that makes sense?\n\n\nhttps://review.openstack.org/#/c/624220/7/keystone/api/projects.py,unified@119",
